{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 9.068,
   "text": "The old hotel in the mountains had one elevator... and one card taped inside it."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 9.668,
   "end": 16.239,
   "text": "After midnight, if this elevator stops on the fifth floor, don't step out. And don't let anyone step in."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 17.039,
   "end": 20.068,
   "text": "I laughed. There were only four buttons."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 21.168,
   "end": 26.949,
   "text": "My first night, I went down for ice around one a.m. The whole hotel was asleep."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 27.549,
   "end": 32.093,
   "text": "On the way back up, the elevator passed four... and kept climbing."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 33.693,
   "end": 34.448,
   "text": "Ding."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 35.848,
   "end": 42.333,
   "text": "The doors opened on a hallway I'd never seen. Green wallpaper. One bare bulb, swinging slowly."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 43.133,
   "end": 48.765,
   "text": "A bellhop stood there in an old red uniform, holding a suitcase. My suitcase."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 49.665,
   "end": 52.822,
   "text": "Your room is ready, he said. Just step out."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 54.122,
   "end": 58.922,
   "text": "I didn't move. I pressed the close button... again, and again, and again."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 59.722,
   "end": 64.458,
   "text": "He never stepped forward. He just smiled... as the doors slid shut."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 65.658,
   "end": 70.629,
   "text": "The elevator sank back down to four. I let out a breath. I was alone."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 71.629,
   "end": 77.432,
   "text": "The doors opened on my floor... and from the corner right behind me, a polite voice said..."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 79.032,
   "end": 80.141,
   "text": "After you."
  }
 ],
